{"uid":"682641a519c4b32a","name":"test_a_state_with_exactly_one_legal_edge_never_calls_ask","fullName":"tests.test_router#test_a_state_with_exactly_one_legal_edge_never_calls_ask","historyId":"115b235486758df517d83504dbdb9a87","time":{"start":1791921468807,"stop":1791921468808,"duration":1},"description":"A state with only one legal edge is unambiguous by construction --\n    `decide()` never reaches `ask`, whatever the caller passes it. This is\n    what makes task 015's single-edge generic-hat path (still the common\n    case: every real, currently-shipped state either has one of the four\n    hand-written `_step_*` guards computing its edge directly from disk\n    state, or -- like this fixture -- exactly one legal edge) provably free\n    of router calls; the engine-level test in test_router_engine.py proves\n    the SAME property end to end through a real dispatch loop, over the\n    real, shipped table (planning/worker/review/replan), where the guard is\n    computed from state rather than the edge count -- both properties are\n    real and are asserted where each is actually true.","descriptionHtml":"<p>A state with only one legal edge is unambiguous by construction --<br />\n<code>decide()</code> never reaches <code>ask</code>, whatever the caller passes it. This is<br />\nwhat makes task 015's single-edge generic-hat path (still the common<br />\ncase: every real, currently-shipped state either has one of the four<br />\nhand-written <code>_step_*</code> guards computing its edge directly from disk<br />\nstate, or -- like this fixture -- exactly one legal edge) provably free<br />\nof router calls; the engine-level test in test_router_engine.py proves<br />\nthe SAME property end to end through a real dispatch loop, over the<br />\nreal, shipped table (planning/worker/review/replan), where the guard is<br />\ncomputed from state rather than the edge count -- both properties are<br />\nreal and are asserted where each is actually true.</p>\n","status":"pass